od type data  on  all of our donors as well as under any  underlying conditions  in these individuals so the first thing  that we wanted to do was assess their  anti-spike antibody levels and we use  this using a cell-based system  whereby we transfected 293ts with the  sarskovi-2 spike protein  this then expresses the protein on its  surface and allows for  detection by donor-derived igg  this igg was purified igg from these  convalescent donors  we then come in with an anti-human igg  antibody that has a fluorescence marker  on it and we can then detect the level  of  of antibodies via fluorescence uh flow  cytometry  so we can see here that we have very  little background on  a negative sample whereas even with  low samples we get good resolution  and detection this is true also for  samples that have intermediate levels of  anti-spike binding as well as  high levels of anti-spike binding  so in you can see here that the  resolution of the assay  is very good where uh the negative  sera is giving us about a two log  difference between  uh the lowest positive sample that we  see here  and we have about a two log resolution  between the  lowest co b2 positive sample  antibodies positive sample and the  highest  we can further see a breakdown of this  here where you see the spectrum of  anti-spike antibody levels in these  convalescent individuals  importantly in these four individuals  with red arrows  they actually tested negative on  commercial tests um  these tests are normally uh these were  elisa based  tests and they actually said that these  individuals were negative  however um we were able to pick them up  with our assay which  is evidence that our assay is very  sensitive even detecting low levels  and since we have a two log difference  between real negative samples and low  level positive samples we're fairly  confident at these results  also these individuals did also test pcr  positive for stars kobe 2.  so we also collected a symptomology  of these infected individuals and so you  can see here the list of symptoms  attached to a severity score  we asked each of our donors to  self-report  the severity of each of these symptoms  what this allowed us to do is come up  with a composite  a total severity score for each  individual while each individual did not  have every single one of these symptoms  they had a various array of symptoms and  we could add those scores up to a total  composite score  when we did that and compare that to the  anti-spike levels we saw that the cohort  pretty much divided into mild versus  moderate  in scores that were above 45 and  below 45. so we then use this to look at  anti-spike levels and saw that the  anti-spike levels were significantly  higher  in individuals that had severity scores  of above 45.  so next we wanted to assess the level of  fc gamma receptor signaling in these  convalescent individuals  and we again expressed sars cov2 and  incubated with uh donor derived igg  except this time we co-cultured these  cells with reporter cell lines that  expressed fc receptor cells on their  surface  upon igg detection these cells  cross-link fc receptor  causing a signaling to occur and  luciferase production  we then can detect luciferase production  as a surrogate marker for level of fc  activation  so in doing this we see that there is  enhanced  fc gamma 2 and fc gamma 3  in convalescent donors with severity  scores above 45.  further when we looked at the level of  fc gamma uh signaling in contrast to the  level of  kobi2 antibody binding we found a  significant correlation  however with fc gamma 3 this correlation  was very striking it seemed  almost like a completely linear  correlation where the level  of anti-spike antibody um  very well correlated with the level of  fc gamma receptor signaling  so what this implies at least with this  small  cohort of convalescent individuals is  that fc gamma receptor  signaling goes up in proportion with the  level of anti-spike  antibodies um so  this was very nice in a a set of  convalescent individuals however  we wanted to see how this was reflected  in the hospitalized population  and through a collaboration with sarad  mahandra of mount sinai  we were able to get a handful of  hospitalized individuals  we also looked at their level of  anti-spike binding and what you can see  here  is the level of anti-spike binding in  low versus  high individuals and we also see here  what it looks like in a severe igg  individual and you can see how there's a  marked elevation in the level of  anti-spike antibody binding  when we graph our convalescent cohort  in comparison to hospitalized  individuals we see that there's a very  significant elevation in anti-spike  antibodies in hospitalized  severe and hospitalized individuals and  this is almost a log  um a log full  a log higher as compared to the mean of  our convalescent cohort  when we further divide the level of  anti-spike  antibody levels in those with severity  scores below 45  above 45 and compared to the severe and  hospitalized individuals you see this  clear stair step  in the level of anti-spike antibody  so we next having seen this elevation  and anti-spike  even beyond our cohor our convalescent  cohort levels we wanted to see what the  level of fce gamma receptor activation  was in these patients  and what we observed was with fc gamma 2  we did see a trend towards significantly  higher fc gamma 2  and we did see significantly higher fc  gamma 3 activation  so it does look as if both anti-spike  and fc gamma receptor activation  correlates with severity of covid19  so what we have here is we're left with  a question  of are there likely ade effects in  covid19  and what we've observed is an increase  in the titers of anti-spike antibodies  however we've seen an increase in afghan  receptor signaling  but it's nowhere near the full  difference that we observed  in the level of anti-spike antibody  binding so  we think that while these in vitro  results are very interesting  in vivo results are in vivo studies are  warranted  with the important caveat that with hiv  and ebola  there are in vitro correlates that have  not panned out  in vivo with ade effects so  in summary fc gamma receptor activation  in uh viral infections we've seen that  efficient fc gamma receptor activation  correlates with the ig mediated control  and clearance  of infections in vivo however with some  pathogens such as dengue  enhanced iggfc interactions may actually  exacerbate disease  with covid19 we've seen that  anti-spike antibody levels correlate  with disease severity scores  in convalescent individuals and also  high levels of fc gamma 3 and fc gamma 2  activation correlate with higher  anti-spike levels in both convalescent  and severe hospitalized individuals  so lastly i'd just like to take a moment  to acknowledge  some of the people doing this fantastic  work that we've been doing  um at i-core biologics so the cohort  samples were gathered and consented  through our company i-core biologics and  this project was spearheaded  by our chief scientific officer jose  luis garrido  with help from our our great staff of  felipe nicole sarah and  sheila i'd also like to thank our  collaborators surab mahandra at mount  sinai for  the hospitalized sample as well as our  collaborator mary  marianas baria and mario calgo  who are currently collecting more  samples for us to process and i'd like  to give a special thanks to all of our  blood donors  thank you
 

